    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves are anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97), who both benefit immensely from a favorable matchup against Pfaadt. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset, with his base projection bolstered by a significant SP skill advantage, while **Andy Pages** thrives today due to a combination of favorable park factors and the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher, which provides an ideal green light for potential stolen base opportunities. **Jacob Wilson** also earns a strong recommendation (69.79) as he capitalizes on a high-ceiling matchup against Bennett, buoyed by the wind and a prime spot in the two-hole. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces an elite arm in deGrom, his strong platoon edge and leadoff positioning keep his efficiency score (60.75) well above our starting threshold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Heliot Ramos** (46.60), who narrowly missed the cut. Despite a solid base projection, he is running into a buzzsaw in Sale, and the drop in efficiency against such an elite arm forced him out of the starting lineup in favor of players with softer matchups. We are also closely monitoring the risks associated with our bottom-tier starters; **Sam Antonacci** (46.72) is firmly in the marginal category today, as his efficiency is severely hampered by a poor matchup against Williams. Furthermore, we continue to play without the depth of **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, the former still sidelined by injury. Managers should note that **Luis Robert Jr.** (59.58) carries a slight risk due to the opposing backstop's elite pop time, which slightly offsets the benefit of his favorable matchup against Chandler. We remain committed to maximizing our speed profile, prioritizing the stolen base upside of **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages** to maintain our competitive edge in this scarcity-driven category.",
